# ttychatter C changelog

## 0.2.0-c-cli

### Added
- Demo mode with `--demo`
- Local demo model catalog for `--demo --models`
- Demo model-cache writer through `--demo --update-models`
- Demo model testing through `--demo --test-model MODEL`
- Demo file-in/file-out chat responses without API key or network access
- Demo response containing both short inline code and long extracted code block
- Model favorites file support
- `--favorites`
- `--favorite-model MODEL`
- `--unfavorite-model MODEL`
- Leading favorite marker in model list output
- `MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE` config key
- `--config` to show active paths and major settings
- `--set KEY VALUE` to write config values
- `--unset KEY` to remove config keys
- `--search-sessions TEXT` for local session-log searching
- Expanded walkthrough covering demo mode and favorites
- Expanded man page entries for demo mode, favorites, config editing, and session search

### Changed
- Version updated to `0.2.0-c-cli`
- User agent updated to `ttychatter-c-cli/0.2`
- Model listing now marks favorites with `*`
- C command-line client is closer to the Bash/Python feature set while preserving Unix file-in/file-out behavior

### Fixed
- Corrected attachment handling hazard found during the feature pass
- Re-tested demo response path with code-block extraction

### Notes
- Demo mode exists so users can test the client without spending provider requests.
- Favorites are deliberately stored as a plain newline-delimited file for easy editing and repair.
- This version remains a command-line client, not an ncurses UI.

## 0.1.0-c-cli

### Added
- Initial C command-line ttychatter client
- Traditional file-in/file-out workflow: `ttychatter input.txt output.log`
- OpenRouter chat-completions support through libcurl
- JSON request/response handling through json-c
- XDG-style config/cache/data defaults
- Config file loading from `~/.config/ttychatter/config`
- Environment API-key support through `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and `TTYCHATTER_API_KEY`
- Plaintext API-key setup command
- Optional GPG-encrypted API-key setup command
- API-key forget command
- Doctor diagnostics command
- Model cache update command
- Model listing from cache
- Model search filter
- Model type filter for routers/fixed/free/auto
- Single-model test command
- Input file to output session log workflow
- Session continuation by reusing the same output file
- Context reconstruction from recent output-file turns
- Repeatable `--attach` / `-a` option
- Text attachment insertion
- Image attachment data URL support for compatible models
- Long fenced-code-block extraction into attachment files
- Loopback output mode for piping AI responses to stdout
- Traditional Unix man page
- Step-by-step WALKTHROUGH document
- Verbose maintainer comments in source code

### Notes
- This is not an ncurses client.
- This version intentionally starts with traditional command-line semantics.
- Non-image binary attachments are listed but not fully embedded yet.
- Encrypted API-key storage uses the external `gpg` command rather than linking a crypto library.
